<title>JAPAN: Indonesia allocates about 250,000 bpd of May crude.</title>
<headline>Indonesia allocates about 250,000 bpd of May crude.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state-owned Pertamina has allocated about 250,000 barrels per day (bpd) of crude for export in May, compared with about 257,800 to 262,800 bpd the previous month, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Minas allocation was about 73,000 bpd of crude for export in May, up from 61,000 bpd in April, they said.</p>
<p>The Duri allocation was 60,000 bpd, up from 70,700 bpd in April.</p>
<p>Industry sources said the following allocations of Pertamina's key grades were made:</p>
<p>(Figures are in barrels per day)</p>
<p>		 May	   April</p>
<p>Minas	  73,000	61,000</p>
<p>Duri	   60,000	70,700</p>
<p>Cinta	  14,000	14,200</p>
<p>Widuri	 18,000	16,800</p>
<p>Arun	   24,000	30,700</p>
<p>Belida	 10,000	12,000</p>
<p>Bontang Mix  35,000	27,400</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3706</p>
</text>
